ng \u0026 AI","description":"Machine Learning \u0026 AI","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:22+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#case-study","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Case Study","description":"Case Study","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#panorama","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"AWS Panorama","description":"AWS Panorama","dateCreated":"2021-11-17T07:15:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:53+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#customer-segment#enterprise","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#customer-segment","name":"Enterprise","description":"Enterprise","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:39:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-05T01:27:39+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#ips-chile-case-study","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"ips-chile-case-study","dateCreated":"2022-07-16T00:00:35+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-07-16T00:02:00+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"The Instituto de Previsión Social (IPS), or Social Security Institute, is responsible for bringing various social benefits to people in Chile. In January of 2022, following the approval of the Universal Guaranteed Pension (PGU), IPS needed a rapid process for its digital platform to simultaneously support consultations for about 2 million people—and be available to receive benefit applications. Using Amazon Web Services (AWS) was key to making this platform available to citizens in just 6 days and to meet user demands, as the number of requests increased by almost 900 percent.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/ips_logo%401x.cc9bc8f32c0a286472544da6c45cae82b196a35a.png","displayLocation":"Chile","customerNameLower":"instituto de previsión social (ips)","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"General Public Services","sortDate":