ry#healthcare-lifesciences","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#industry","name":"healthcare-lifesciences","description":"\u003cp\u003eThis tag is initially being created specifically for the Directory Cards componenet on aws.amazon.com/health/case-studies/. When the GCRP decided to add multilingual content to the CSDIR in 2023, the owners of this page only wanted to display the English content in our Directory. Because the Directory Cards component on their page uses an OR operator to pull in content from two tags, they would be unable to add a prefilter condition to look for only English content. This can only be done if the page is using an AND operator. Thus, this tag will be autoapplied to all content that meets the current prefilter conditions. At that point, the page owners can use the AND operator to display content with this tag and GLOBAL#language#english.\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#pearson-uses-amazon-fsx-for-netapp-ontap-video","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"pearson-uses-amazon-fsx-for-netapp-ontap-video","dateCreated":"2022-05-14T20:14:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-05-14T20:15:16+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"By migrating to Amazon Web Services (AWS) and using Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP, Pearson improves agility and performance of their enterprise resource planning application. With AWS, Pearson can spend time focusing on its user journey without worrying about operational overhead.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/pearson-logo%401x.3d48da03240be6fda73055c8c28858804f1504b0.png","displayLocation":"United States","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Media \u0026 Entertainment","sortDate":"2022-05-13","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/pearson-uses-amazon-fsx-for-netapp-ontap-video/?did\u003dcr_card